# Google Places API (New): place photos and Google star ratings.
# Used only by the Supabase place-photo function, on the server. Never put it in the app or Config/.
#
# To get one: Google Cloud console -> pick or create a project -> turn on billing
# -> APIs & Services -> Library -> enable "Places API (New)"
# -> Credentials -> Create credentials -> API key.
# Restrict the key to "Places API (New)" only. Leave application restrictions on None (server-side use).
# Setting a small budget alert under Billing -> Budgets & alerts is a good idea.
#
# Copy this file to supabase/functions/.env and paste your key below. That file is gitignored; never commit a real key.
# Without a key, places fall back to visit photos and the map, and no Google ratings are shown.
GOOGLE_PLACES_KEY=XXX

# GitHub: opens an issue (labelled bug and user-reported-bug) for each bug report sent from the app.
# Used only by the bug-report-issue function, on the server. Never put it in the app or Config/.
#
# To get one (the repo owner has to make it, since fine-grained tokens only reach repos you own):
# GitHub -> Settings -> Developer settings -> Personal access tokens -> Fine-grained tokens -> Generate new token.
# Resource owner: larkindaniel. Repository access: only roam. Permissions: Issues -> Read and write, nothing else.
#
# The repo is public: issues carry the description, screenshots, device and a SQL query for the steps, never who sent it.
# Without these, reports are still saved in Supabase; no issue is opened. For the hosted beta, set them with
# supabase secrets set GITHUB_TOKEN=... GITHUB_REPO=larkindaniel/roam --project-ref xnjzuotytfzyppubjcfi
GITHUB_TOKEN=XXX
GITHUB_REPO=larkindaniel/roam
